--- a/docs/Reference/Validation-and-Serialization.md
+++ b/docs/Reference/Validation-and-Serialization.md
@@ -164,6 +164,28 @@ Validations can be a complete JSON Schema object with a `type` of `'object'` and
 a `'properties'` object containing parameters, or a simpler variation listing
 parameters at the top level.
 
+### Default schemas
+
+An instance can apply default request-part schemas to every route it registers
+with `setDefaultSchema`. A route that declares the same part overrides the
+default for that part; the remaining parts keep the default.
+
+```js
+const fastify = Fastify()
+fastify.setDefaultSchema({
+  headers: {
+    type: 'object',
+    required: ['x-api-key']
+  }
+})
+
+// Every route registered on this instance now requires `x-api-key`, unless the
+// route declares its own `headers` schema.
+```
+
+The defaults apply to the instance the method is called on and to its
+encapsulated plugins. Calling it again replaces the previous defaults.
+
 > ℹ For using the latest Ajv (v8), refer to the
 > [`schemaController`](./Server.md#schema-controller) section.
 
